Plan `{{ v('ch8.plan_hash') }}`. {{ v('ch8.method.estimator') }}; {{ v('ch8.method.interval') }}; {{ v('ch8.method.split') }}; {{ v('ch8.method.family') }}. Three operating points have their interior tests on the data page: the line ({{ v('policy.affordable_lines') }}) is {{ v('ch8.line_degenerate') }}, the down payment ({{ v('policy.down_payment_shares') }}) is {{ v('ch8.down_degenerate') }}, and the saving rate ({{ v('policy.saving_rates') }}) is printed beside them. On the simulator the breakeven is graded as late arriving truth: the estimate made from the history to a stated year against the breakeven the realised path produced, with a mean error of {{ v('recovery.breakeven_horizon.mean_bias') }} years and {{ v('recovery.breakeven_horizon.mean_flag_rate') }} interval coverage; the simulated decade after the estimate held a boom the history did not, which is the caveat on every breakeven here.
